=== Generic symbolic check: closure under (q, x) <-> (c, X) involution ===

For a generic rational (x, y) on E_PCP(q) (with y^2 = x(x+1)(x+q^2)):
  c = 2qy/(q^2-x^2)
  sqrt(1+c^2) = (x^2+2q^2 x + q^2)/(q^2-x^2)        [identity 1]
  sqrt(q^2+c^2) = q(x^2 + 2x + q^2)/(q^2-x^2)       [identity 2]

The Euler brick (1, q, c) has 3 rational face diagonals:
  d = sqrt(1+q^2)    (constant in x)
  e = sqrt(q^2+c^2)  (formula above)
  f = sqrt(1+c^2)    (formula above)

=== Symbolic involution: birational map E_PCP(q) <-> E_PCP(c) ===

Given (x, y) on E_PCP(q), compute c = 2qy/(q^2-x^2).
Then on E_PCP(c) the corresponding X satisfies (canonically) one of 4 roots of the quartic above.

Symbolic insight: the Euler brick (1, q, c) is encoded by
  a = 1, b = q, c = c  (edges)
with rational face diagonals d, e, f as above.

By symmetry of the brick: swap b <-> c. Then we want (1, c, q) as a brick.
  i.e., E_PCP(c) at a parameter X with 2cY/(c^2-X^2) = q.

Symbolic: with c = 2qy/(q^2-x^2), back-substitute into the quartic and look
for a polynomial identity.
